 ],
 "literal": "May I see indeed the husband, eyes to be filled; having seen after, will depart my soft shoulders' pallor.",
 "translation": "May I but behold my lord so that my eyes are filled with his sight; once I have seen him, the sallow pallor of separation will vanish from my soft shoulders.",
 "modern": "என் கண்கள் குளிரும் வரை என் தலைவனை நான் காண்பேனாக! அவனைக் கண்ட பிறகு, என் மென்மையான தோள்களில் படர்ந்துள்ள பசலை நிறம் நீங்கிவிடும்.",
 "explanation": "The heroine expresses her intense longing to gaze upon her lover, whom she addresses as the lord of the shore (கொண்கன்). She wishes to look at him until her eyes are completely satisfied (கண்ணார). She is certain that once she beholds him, the sickly yellow-green pallor (பசப்பு) that has spread over her soft shoulders (மென்தோள்) due to the pain of separation will instantly disappear.",
